celeste-linux (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bug-fix update from two adversarial reviews: the filesystem gate now
    refuses hard-linked files; spontaneous deliveries keep their re-armed
    successor; settings recovery never logs the file's contents; all
    helper-process reads are deadline-bounded; MCP transports survive a
    wedged server or a timed-out request and rethrow cancellation; approval
    timeouts are reported accurately; shared payloads land visibly; persona
    names cannot inject .desktop keys; same-session float settings read back
    correctly.
  * Version bumped to 0.2.0.

 -- Nikos <nikos@localhost>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:40:14 +0300

celeste-linux (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: the jpackage app image with its own trimmed runtime under
    /usr/lib/celeste-linux, the application menu entry, the hicolor icon and the
    systemd user unit (installed, not enabled). The ONNX Runtime jar is cut to
    the platform this package can load, 90 MB -> 5.7 MB, and the build refuses
    to proceed if the cut has nothing to cut (PLAN.md §4, §10/M6).

 -- Nikos <nikos@localhost>  Thu, 16 Oct 2026 21:20:00 +0300
